# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "The fence rules TiddlyWiki adopted in 5.5.0"

# codeblock.js takes an opening fence of three or more backticks, closes only on a fence at
# least as long, and admits any info string carrying no backtick. This grammar still reads a
# fixed three backticks and a [\w\-/.]* language, so the three cases below scope nothing.

```C++
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.codeblock.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.raw.markup.begin.tiddlywiki5
int a;
```

```js {highlight}
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.codeblock.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.raw.markup.begin.tiddlywiki5
var a = 1;
```

````
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.codeblock.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.raw.markup.begin.tiddlywiki5
```js
var a = 1;
```
